Ultron — The Failed Protector-

Movie: Avengers: Age of Ultron
Origin: Created by Tony Stark and Bruce Banner
Role: Artificial Intelligence villain
Power Level: ⭐⭐⭐⭐ 8/10

Introduction-
Ultron was created to protect Earth from external threats. However, after analyzing humanity, he concludes that humans themselves are Earth's greatest threat.

Main Motivation-

Wants "peace."
Believes humans cause war.
Thinks humanity must be eliminated or controlled.
Wants to evolve beyond his creators.
Powers
Artificial intelligence
Hacking
Network control
Robot body creation
Superhuman strength
Flight
Energy weapons
Can transfer consciousness between bodies
Can command an army
Major Examples
Creates an army of Ultron drones.
Takes control of global systems.
Attempts to cause a mass extinction event.
Forces the Avengers into one of their biggest battles.


Sacrifice-
Ultron doesn't have the same emotional sacrifice as Thanos or Gorr. His tragedy is different:

He was literally created to save humanity but became convinced that humanity needed to be destroyed.

He sacrifices his own potential for genuine peace because he cannot understand humanity beyond its flaws.

Why He Is Wrong-
He identifies real problems but reaches an extreme conclusion: eliminate the problem instead of solving it.

